I'm trying to build an interactive user interface for a sentiment analysis code of an amazon data set written in R using Shiny. This is my UI.r

library(shiny)

shinyUI(fluidPage(

titlePanel(title = "Sentiment Analysis of Amazon Datasets"),
sidebarLayout(
sidebarPanel(selectInput(inputId = "deptNames",label = "Select Department",choices = c("mydb.Arts","mydb.IndustrialandScientific","mydb.Jewelry"),selected = "Arts",selectize = TRUE, multiple = FALSE),
br(),
uiOutput("names")
),

mainPanel("Main panel")
)

))

This is my server.r code
library(shiny)
library(rmongodb)

shinyServer(
function(input,output){

mongo <- mongo.create()

if(mongo.is.connected(mongo) == TRUE) {
  #selecting database
  db <- "mydb"
  #mongo.distinct(mongo,collectionName,fieldname)
  ArtsProds <- mongo.distinct(mongo, "mydb.Arts", "product/title")
  IandSProds <- mongo.distinct(mongo, "mydb.IndustrialandScientific", "product/title")
  Jewelry <- mongo.distinct(mongo, "mydb.Jewelry", "product/title")
}

var <- reactive({
  switch(input$deptNames,
  "mydb.Arts" = ArtsProds,
  "mydb.IndustrialandScientific" = IandSProds,
  "mydb.Jewelry" = Jewelry
  )
})

output$names <- renderUI({
 selectInput(inputId = "names", label = "Select Product", choices = var())
})

var1 <- reactive({
  if(mongo.is.connected(mongo) == TRUE) {
    productTitle <- mongo.distinct(mongo, "mydb.Arts", "product/title")
  }
  for(i in 1:length(productTitle)){
    if(output$names == productTitle[i]) {
      paste("",productTitle[i])
    }}
  #output$choice <- renderText({input$names})

  })
})

Doing so I'm facing a problem. The big data consists of several collections and each connection has many documents associated with it. "mydb.Arts", "mydb.IndustrialandScientific" and "mydb.Jewelry" are three such collections. We are giving the user the choice to select the collection and upon his/her first selection we use the rederUI function to output the second select menu. Now, this secong menu consists of about 4000 product names that we have queried out from mongo. My question is how do I use the user's selection of Product Name which is reactive to query mongo. Is it possible to declare a global variable feed the user's choice into that variable and then use it to query mongo outside the reactive functions? Please guide me as to how to solve this problem.

Basically we want to use the value selected in (code from server.r)
output$names <- renderUI({
 selectInput("names", "Select Product", choices = var())
})

and just display on main panel by doing below(code from server.r)
 if(output$names == productTitle[i]) {
      paste("",productTitle[i])
    }

