Note that you don't have to nest the lists:

> output$foo <- renderUI({
>         LL = list()
>         LL[[1]] = list(sliderInput('a',"a description",min=0,max=200,value=c(50,150)))
>         LL[[2]] = list(sliderInput('b',"b description",min=0,max=200,value=c(50,150)))
>         return(LL)
>     })
>

should just be:

> output$foo <- renderUI({
>   list(

>     sliderInput('a',"a description",min=0,max=200,value=c(50,150)),
>     sliderInput('b',"b description",min=0,max=200,value=c(50,150))
>   )
> })

You can also use lapply, that's a perfectly fine way to generate a list of tags.

