You probably shouldn't be assigning an output value in the observer. I think it's probably executing fullTimeInfo() once when the observer is triggered, and then one more time when the new renderPlot() is called.

      observe({
        if(input$samp > 0) {
          fullTimeInfo(input$term1, input$term2)
          output$compare <- renderPlot({
            fullTimeInfo()
          })
        }
      })

I suggest pulling the renderPlot() outside of the observe() if possible.

