It’s in Trelliscope.  So it’s a bit complex (and a bit ugly at the moment).  It’s called in $(document).ready().

https://github.com/hafen/trelliscope/blob/master/inst/trelliscopeViewer/www/assets/custom/main.js#L511-L512

But even if I call bind and unbind manually from the javascript console long after the page is loaded, the elements still do not register using shiny 0.12.

Is there some other attribute of shiny output divs that gets effected with initShiny?  For example are data attributes added during init to the divs that would cause bind and unbind to dismiss the output divs that show up after init is called as valid outputs?

Ryan

